title Login, OTP second factor, session mint, and refresh rotation

actor Customer as user
participant "BFF\n(authentication module)" as bff
database "Valkey" as valkey
participant "SMTP\n(Mailpit in dev)" as smtp
database "bff-db\n(refresh_tokens)" as db
participant "Fineract Core" as fineract

user -> bff : POST /api/v1/authentication/login\n{email, password} + X-Device-Fingerprint
bff -> bff : user BOUND? password matches?\n(any failure: same generic 401)
bff -> valkey : store SHA-256(OTP), TTL 300s
bff -> smtp : email the 6-character OTP
bff --> user : challenge token (5 min JWT,\npurpose=2fa_challenge, fingerprint claim)

user -> bff : POST /api/v1/authentication/2fa\n{challenge token, OTP} + X-Device-Fingerprint
bff -> bff : verify purpose claim +\nfingerprint claim == header
bff -> valkey : validate OTP hash (max 5 attempts),\ndelete on success (single use)
group establishSession (shared mint path)
  bff -> fineract : GET /clients/{id} live standing check\n(uncached, fail closed, status must be 300)
  bff -> db : store SHA-256(refresh token)\n+ device fingerprint + expiry
end
bff --> user : Set-Cookie access_token (15 min JWT)\n+ refresh_token (rotating, HttpOnly)

... later, access token near expiry ...

user -> bff : POST /api/v1/authentication/refresh\nrefresh_token cookie + X-Device-Fingerprint
bff -> db : look up token hash; require unexpired,\nunrevoked, fingerprint == stored binding
note right of bff
  Rotation: old row revoked, rotated_to links successor.
  Replay of a rotated token: same-device within 30s
  grace forks a session; otherwise all of the user's
  refresh tokens are revoked as theft.
end note
bff -> fineract : KYC live check again (every mint)
bff --> user : new access_token + rotated refresh_token cookies

@enduml
